-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",406,{
[12961]="7004A8F5\n1\tPatrol Iant Angos \"in search of the Elf-warrior\"\tIant Angos can be found to the south-east of Cirith Ungol in Lhingris. Captain Róglarg has asked you to patrol Iant Angos in search of the Elf-warrior on the run in Lhingris. You should travel to the bridge of Iant Angos.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have patrolled Iant Angos.\n",
[12962]="7004A8FC\n1\tPatrol Torech Ungol \"in search of the Elf-warrior\"\tTorech Ungol can be found up the pathway south-west of Cirith Ungol in the heights of the Ephel Dúath. Captain Róglarg has asked you to patrol Torech Ungol, Shelob's Lair, in search of the Elf-warrior on the run in Lhingris. You should travel to Torech Ungol, but remain on guard.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have patrolled Torech Ungol.\n",
[12963]="70018C28\n1\tGather mistletoe (total: 5)\tMistletoe can be found on the young fir-trees along the northern road to Thrasi's Lodge. Saervereth asked you to gather some mistletoe for her so she may remember what it is Yule is all about.\n2\tBring the mistletoe to Saervereth in Duillond\tSaervereth is at Duillond, in the Festival area. Saervereth will be eager to see the mistletoe and muse on the true meaning of Yule.\n",
[12964]="70042F59\n1\tSearch for the lost Ranger outside the Palace of Eldacar\tThe Palace of Eldacar can be found due west of Halhir in western Osgiliath. Halhir has asked you to search near the Palace of Eldacar for a lost ally.\n2\tSearch the Palace of Eldacar for the lost Ranger\tThe Palace of Eldacar can be found due west of Halhir in western Osgiliath. You have not found Halhir's ally, and should now search within the ruins of the Palace.\n3\tExamine the slain Ranger\tThe Palace of Eldacar can be found due west of Halhir in western Osgiliath. You have spotted a crumpled body in the distance. You should examine it before leaving the Palace.\n4\tTalk to Halhir\tHalhir can be found due east of the Palace of Eldacar in western Osgiliath. You have found Halhir's slain ally, and should now return to him bearing the news of his friend's passing.\n",
[12965]="7005B223\n1\tObtain bat bait from an Orc beast-master\tThe Orc village Dalugronk is located on the lowest level of Deepscrave, to the north-east of Aslíf. The Orc beast-masters may have bait that you can use to lure out the bat Sumri.\n2\tLure out and defeat Sumri\tYou have obtained bait to lure Sumri out.\n3\tTalk to Elta near Shataz-kordh\tYou have defeated Sumri. Elta waits for you nearby to the north-west, watching the worm nest Shataz-kordh.\n",
[12966]="70002D16\n1\tAccept Donnan's challenge\tDonnan and his brother are at Aughaire on the west side of the Hillman town, awaiting your response to their challenge. Arzhur has asked you once again to fight against the challengers from a hostile clan loyal to Angmar.\n2\tArzhur is at Aughaire You should return to Arzhur with news of your victory against the second challenge.\t\n",
[12967]="7000007A\n1\tFind the missing second gear\tThe chest containing the second gear can be found on the south side of the goblin-infested ruins in the Vale of Thráin, south of Thorin's Halls and west of Noglond. Bávor discovered the location of the second gear and has sent you to search for it, while he repairs the first gear.\n2\tBring the second gear to Bávor\030Collect Gear\tBávor is in Thorin's Hall. Bávor will be pleased to begin working with the second gear.\n",
[12968]="700572FA\n1\tInspect the illusion of the second stone\tAn illusion has appeared before you in the Crown Chamber. You should inspect the illusion of the second stone.\n2\tFind the second stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n3\tFind the second stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n4\tTalk to the Emissary\tYou have found a hidden chamber in the Mountains of Shadow, but a Nameless entity stands in your way.\n5\tFind the first remnant\030Find the second remnant\030Find the third remnant\030Find the fourth remnant\030Find the fifth remnant\030Find the sixth remnant\030Find the seventh remnant\tThe Emissary has asked you to find the \"Remnants of the Fallen Ones\" and return them.\n6\tTalk to the Emissary and 'Speak the Words'\tYou have collected the remnants for the Emissary. You should return to the Emissary and 'Speak the Words'.\n7\tReturn the stone to its pedestal\tYou have found one of the missing stones! You should return them to their rightful place in the Crown Chamber.\n",
[12969]="7001752A\n1\tFind and eliminate the source of Lar's worry\tThe Sixteenth Hall lies to the north-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Lar has asked you to delve deep into the Sixteenth Hall and see if you can locate the source of his unease.\n2\tRetrurn to Lar at the Shadowed Refuge\tLar can be found in the Shadowed Refuge, south-west of the Sixteenth Hall. You should return to Lar and tell him what you discovered and slew: a terrible headless creature in the depths of the hall, lurking in a room full of spores and slime.\n",
[12970]="7006595F\n1\tCollect savoury herbs (total: 8)\tJódha has asked you to pick some savoury herbs outside of Pelargir. Find herbs in the fields west of Pelargir.\n2\tTalk to Jódha\tYou have found enough herbs to satisfy Jódha. Deliver the savoury herbs to Jódha.\n",
[12971]="700444E9\n1\tLook for the key (total: 6)\tThe Wrights' Fellow-hall lies on the far southern end of the First Circle. Bergil knows of a second, unwatched door into the Cisterns, which might grant the children passage directly to the Fourth Circle. A key to it was lost near the Wrights' Fellow-hall recently. Search for it in that area.\n2\tFound the key\tFound the key.\n3\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil waits in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. Tell Bergil you found the key to the cisterns' hidden door. With it, the children might find passage directly to the Fourth Circle.\n4\tTalk to Gelwen\tGelwen stands in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. Bergil says two other children, Gelwen and Glatham, would like to join you in searching the cisterns for the secret passage. He suggested that you speak with Gelwen herself, first.\n5\tEnter the cisterns through the hidden door\tThe door can be found near the Wrights' Fellow-hall, in the southern stretch of the First Circle. Enter the cisterns through the hidden door.\n6\tTalk to Gelwen\tIf you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you. You have met Bergil, Gelwen, and Glatham in the cisterns. Gelwen has something to say.\n7\tExit into the Fourth Circle\tIf you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you. Explore the cisterns with Bergil, Gelwen, and Glatham, and search for a passage up to the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n8\tTalk to Gelwen\tIf you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you. You have come out of the secret passage through the cisterns, to the Fourth Circle of the City. Gelwen again appears to have something she wishes to say.\n9\tInvestigate the Finding Place\tThe Finding Place lies near the cisterns' exit in the Fourth Circle. The children have spotted something they call the \"Finding Place.\" Walk over to it and see what it is. If you get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call the children to you.\n10\tIf you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you. Show Bergil the slightly crumpled letter you found in the crevice of the Finding Place.\t\n11\tTalk to Bergil\tThe Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. Meet Bergil and the other children back at the Old Guest-house.\n",
[12972]="7005AAFF\n1\tTalk to Hórin outside Bagud-dum and go with him to investigate\tHórin is standing by outside Bagud-dum. You should speak to Hórin and complete 'Instance: The Secret Ritual'.\n2\tTalk to Hórin just outside the door to the keep in Bagud-dum\tHórin has dragged you out of Bagud-dum. You should talk to Hórin.\n3\tComplete 'Apprentices of the Cult' for Hórin\030Complete 'Spirits and Summoners' for Hórin\030Find Loknashra inside the keep of Bagud-dum\tThe Angmarim cultists have taken over the dwarf-fort Bagud-dum. You should complete objectives in Bagud-dum to prevent their plans from reaching fruition.\n4\tTalk to Hórin outside Bagud-dum\tHórin is waiting for you outside Bagud-dum. You should talk to Hórin.\n",
[12973]="70054F37\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir can be found in Falch Gurth. Mithrandir has asked you to accompany him into Thuringwath. You should talk to Mithrandir when you are prepared.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in Thuringwath\tMithrandir can be found in Thuringwath. You have passed through Falch Gurth into Thuringwath with Mithrandir. You should talk to Mithrandir.\n",
[12974]="7004CE2D\n1\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n2\tCollect the dusty tome\tKing Thorin III can be found at his seat in Erebor. You should bring the tome to King Thorin III.\n3\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found at his seat in Erebor. You should bring the tome to King Thorin III.\n",
[12975]="7004E72A\n1\tExamine the spider corpse\tA spider corpse can be found deep within Stormwall, high in the mountains north-east of Skarháld. You should examine the spider corpse.\n2\tTalk to Agátur\tYou should return to Agátur, back in Skarháld.\n",
[12976]="70042F27\n1\tInvestigate the ruins of Tuntham\tThe ruins of Tuntham can be found north-east of Bâr Húrin. You should enter the suspicious building at Tuntham.\n2\tEnter the ruined interior of Tuntham\tThe ruins of Tuntham can be found north-east of Bâr Húrin. You should enter the suspicious building at Tuntham.\n3\tBreak up the Orkish planning committee (total: 3)\tThe ruins of Tuntham can be found north-east of Bâr Húrin. You should defeat the Orkish planning committee you found within one of the buildings in Tuntham.\n4\tDestroy the Orkish plans\tThe ruins of Tuntham can be found north-east of Bâr Húrin. You should destroy the Orkish plans you found within one of the buildings in Tuntham.\n5\tCompleted\tDestroyed the Orkish plans.\n",
[12977]="700033BC\n1\tBring rune-inscribed collar to the Elf near Woodhall\tAn Elf may be camped near Woodhall, south of Budgeford. Linda Bolger was confounded by your discovery of a collar where she had seen the great wolf. She was unable to read the letters on the collar, but thought that perhaps the Elf Milo thought he saw might be able to decipher them.\n",
[12978]="700176CD\n1\tDiscover the entrance to the secret chamber\tThe entrance lies somewhere in Nud-melek, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall, perhaps the Second Hall. Geirfast has asked you to find the entrance to the secret chamber depicted in the shadow-map.\n2\tTalk to Geirfast\tGeirfast is at the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of the Second Hall. You should return to Geirfast to tell him where the chamber is.\n3\tGeirfast is at the Twenty-first Hall. You should speak with Geirfast when you are ready to travel.\t\n4\tTalk to Geirfast in the Twenty-first Hall\tGeirfast is at the Twenty-first Hall. You should return at once to Geirfast.\n5\tTalk to Lenglammel at the Shadowed Refuge\tLenglammel is encamped at the Shadowed Refuge. Geirfast suggested you speak with the Elf Lenglammel.\n",
[12979]="700085DA\n1\tTalk to Nethraw\tThe lore-master Nethraw can be found at the Krúsle Lannan, a considerable distance to the east of Gabilshathûr. Banfuir suggested you speak with the lore-master Nethraw.\n",
[12980]="7005F867\n1\tScout Lochan Dúv with Hersegg\tLochan Dúv can be found to the west of Lugun-nâla in Gloomingtarn. Hersegg has asked you to accompany her in combatting the Iron Crown at Lochan Dúv. You should travel to Lochan Dúv with Hersegg. NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.\n2\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at your side. You have entered Lochan Dúv with Hersegg. You should talk to Hersegg. NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.\n3\tDefeat the Iron Crown commander at Lochan Dúv\030Aid Hersegg with 'Curious Captives'\tThe Iron Crown commander can be found at Lochan Dúv. Hersegg can be found at your side. You should defeat the Iron Crown commander at Lochan Dúv and aid Hersegg with her task. NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.\n4\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at your side. You have defeated the Iron Crown commander and helped to sow discord at Lochan Dúv. You should talk to Hersegg. NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.\n5\tFind the entrance to Mîn Lorg\tThe entrance to Mîn Lorg can be found somewhere within Lochan Dúv in Gloomingtarn. The Iron Crown commander held orders demanding an excavation of Mîn Lorg before the arrival of his master, Allaban the Collector. You should search for the entrance to Mîn Lorg. NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.\n6\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at your side. You have found the entrance to Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg. NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.\n7\tTalk to Hersegg at Mîn Lorg\tHersegg can be found at the entrance to Mîn Lorg within Lochan Dúv in Gloomingtarn. You have found the entrance to Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.\n",
[12981]="70062DD8\n1\tSearch for clues\tRhiangar has asked you to be on the look-out for any signs that her mother may have visited Sarch Vorn. Sarch Vorn is in northern Cardolan.\n2\tBring the necklace to Rhiangar\tYou have found an old necklace on the weather-worn skeleton of a woman. You suspect Rhiangar would be interested in this item. You should bring the necklace to her in Herne.\n",
[12982]="70048C85\n1\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak can be found near Seregost. You should talk to Viznak.\n2\tDefeat merrevail (total: 14)\tViznak has been ambushed by merrevail on Seregost's terrace! You should defeat the merrevail.\n3\tFind an entrance into Seregost\tViznak has been taken into Seregost. You should find a way inside.\n4\tTalk to Rhadrog\tRhadrog is standing by inside the prison. You should talk to Rhadrog.\n5\tTalk to the Nurnhoth prisoner\030Talk to the Easterling prisoner\tLiving prisoners can be found inside the prison. You should talk to these prisoners.\n6\tTalk to Rhadrog\tRhadrog is right next to you! You should talk to Rhadrog.\n7\tTalk to the Uruk Prisoner\tLiving prisoners can be found inside the prison. You should talk to these prisoners.\n8\tFind Viznak\tViznak is somewhere deeper in the prison. Now that you have the information you need, you should find Viznak.\n9\tDefeat the Blood-witch\030Defeat Stained merrevail (total: 2)\tThe Blood-witch can be found in the deepest chamber of Seregost's prison. You should defeat the Blood-witch and her merrevail.\n10\tRun!\tBolvág the Cursed is chasing you! You should run!\n11\tTalk to Rhadrog\tYou have managed to escape with Rhadrog and Viznak. You should talk to Rhadrog.\n",
[12983]="700571C5\n1\tTalk to Agátur outside of Sundergrót\tSundergrót can be found in the Floodfells. You should talk to Agátur outside of Sundergrót.\n2\tTalk to Rúzat at Limlók\030Talk to Agátur at Limlók\030Talk to Náth at Limlók\tRúzat, Agátur, and Náth can be found at Limlók. You should talk to the three dwarves.\n",
[12984]="700718E4\n1\tDefeat wights at Naxar Dâl (total: 4)\tAndûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You should start at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and defeat some wights there to clear some space for yourself.\n2\tAndûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You started at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and defeated some of the wights, clearing some space for yourself.\t\n3\tDefeat wights at Khâb Daku (total: 4)\tAndûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You started at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and should now go to the Crypts of Khâb Daku, to the south. Defeat some of the wights there to clear some space for yourself.\n4\tAndûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You started at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and next went to the Crypts of Khâb Daku, to the south, where you defeated some of the wights there, clearing some space for yourself.\t\n5\tTalk to Andûmu in Gadim-ûn\tAndûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You started at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and next went to the Crypts of Khâb Daku, examining grave goods at each location. You should return to Andûmu in Gadim-ûn and tell him what you discovered.\n",
[12985]="700598DA\n1\tTalk to Marigold\tTom has told you that the sword can be found near Old Man Willow. You should work together with Marigold to find the sword and destroy it.\n2\tComplete 'Woe of the Willow' on any difficulty\tComplete 'Woe of the Willow' on any difficulty. At level 20 or above, use the Instance Finder to enter Woe of the Willow.\n3\tTalk to Hob Hayward\tHob Hayward guards the Buckland Gate. You should tell him what has transpired since you last saw him.\n",
[12986]="70027B59\n1\tCollect digestive roots (total: 6)\tDigestive roots can be found throughout Tâl Methedras, around the shores of the lake and on the eyot in the middle of the water, at the base of trees.\n2\tGrind up the digestive roots at the grinding stone north of Herestan\tThe grinding stone is at the armour-making pavillion north of Herestan. You now have some digestive roots and need to grind them into powder.\n3\tBring the digestive root-powder to Herestan\tHerestan is to the south of the grinding stone, by the lake's edge, where you left him.\n",
[12987]="700681C0\n1\tDefeat sekbiri (total: 8)\tA worried guard at the gate of Halrax has asked you to cull down the sekbir population in their den on the north side of the island. Sekbiri may be found at Ghar Jâdam to the north of Zamarzîr.\n",
[12988]="7005466E\n1\tFind Taurlingol\tAccording to the Rangers, the spider-infested forest of Taurlingol can be found in eastern Cirith Ungol. You should find Taurlingol.\n2\tFind the source of the shouting\tAs you entered Taurlingol, you heard someone shouting. You should find the source of the shouting.\n3\tHelp Atli defeat the spider\tYou have found Atli Spider-bane in combat with a giant spider of Taurlingol. You should help Atli defeat the spider!\n4\tTalk to Atli Spider-bane\tAtli has moved to a safe location nearby. You should find and talk to Atli Spider-bane.\n5\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas is tending to Atli Spider-bane's injuries on an overlook near Taurlingol. You should talk to Legolas.\n6\tHelp Legolas with 'The Daughters of Iphantemel'\030Help Legolas with 'The Trees of Taurlingol'\030Help Atli with 'Before They Become a Problem'\030Help Atli with 'The Only Solution'\tLegolas has asked for your assistance with tasks in Taurlingol. You should complete 'The Daughters of Iphantemel,' 'The Trees of Taurlingol,' 'Before They Become a Problem,' and 'The Only Solution.'\n7\tTalk to Legolas\tYou should inform Legolas of your success defeating the Mirkwood Spiders. Legolas can be found on a hill near Taurlingol.\n",
[12989]="7002FD57\n1\tTalk to Odnoth\tThe two Rohirrim soldiers can be found in Garsfeld proper, and Gísling is inside the Mead Hall. Gísil wants you to speak to his men and his son, Gísling, about what action should be taken to protect Garsfeld in the wake of learning that the town is surrounded by foes.\n2\tTalk to Albryt\tThe two Rohirrim soldiers can be found in Garsfeld proper, and Gísling is inside the Mead Hall. Gísil wants you to speak to his men and his son, Gísling, about what action should be taken to protect Garsfeld in the wake of learning that the town is surrounded by foes.\n3\tTalk to Gísling\tThe two Rohirrim soldiers can be found in Garsfeld proper, and Gísling is inside the Mead Hall. Gísil wants you to speak to his men and his son, Gísling, about what action should be taken to protect Garsfeld in the wake of learning that the town is surrounded by foes.\n4\tTalk to Gísil\tGísil can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld. You should return to Gísil with the opinions of his counsellors.\n",
[12990]="7005718A\n1\tTravel to Thokvist in Misthallow\tThokvist can be found in the south of Misthallow. You should travel to Thokvist.\n2\tTalk to Léothred at Thokvist\tLéothred can be found at Thokvist. You should talk to Léothred.\n3\tDefeat Orcs in Misthallow (total: 6)\tOrcs can be found in Misthallow. You should defeat Orcs in Misthallow.\n4\tTalk to Léothred at Thokvist\tLéothred can be found at Thokvist. You should talk to Léothred.\n",
[12991]="700085E6\n1\tUse Sword-sentinel\030Collect The Sword of Arvedui\tThe statues of the Seven Sentinels are in the Fane of the Seven Sentinels, east of Gabilshathûr. The seven swords must be given to the Seven Sentinels in the correct order before the vault will open.\n2\tUse Sword-sentinel\030Collect The Sword of Rhudaur\tThe statues of the Seven Sentinels are in the Fane of the Seven Sentinels, east of Gabilshathûr. The seven swords must be given to the Seven Sentinels in the correct order before the vault will open.\n3\tUse Sword-sentinel\030Collect The Sword of Gondor\tThe statues of the Seven Sentinels are in the Fane of the Seven Sentinels, east of Gabilshathûr. The seven swords must be given to the Seven Sentinels in the correct order before the vault will open.\n4\tUse Sword-sentinel\030Collect The Sword of Slaughter\tThe statues of the Seven Sentinels are in the Fane of the Seven Sentinels, east of Gabilshathûr. The seven swords must be given to the Seven Sentinels in the correct order before the vault will open.\n5\tUse Sword-sentinel\030Collect The Sword of Sorrow\tThe statues of the Seven Sentinels are in the Fane of the Seven Sentinels, east of Gabilshathûr. The seven swords must be given to the Seven Sentinels in the correct order before the vault will open.\n6\tUse Sword-sentinel\030Collect The Sword of Twilight\tThe statues of the Seven Sentinels are in the Fane of the Seven Sentinels, east of Gabilshathûr. The seven swords must be given to the Seven Sentinels in the correct order before the vault will open.\n7\tUse Sword-sentinel\030Collect The Sword of the Vigil\tThe statues of the Seven Sentinels are in the Fane of the Seven Sentinels, east of Gabilshathûr. The seven swords must be given to the Seven Sentinels in the correct order before the vault will open.\n8\tBring the treasure of the Seven Sentinels back to Nethraw\030Collect the treasure of the Seven Sentinels\tYou have solved the puzzle of the seven sentinels, so now it is time to enter the vault and retrieve the treasure.\n",
[12992]="7000D779\n1\tUse Pedestal\tNethraw is at the Krúsle Lannan, east of Gabilshathur. You must place the Seven Swords in their pedestals to open the Krúsle Lannan.\n2\tTalk to Nethraw\tSearch the Krúslë Lannan with Nethraw.\n3\tEscape from Krúslë Lannan\tYou must escape from the Krúslë Lannan with Nethraw.\n",
})
